<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eudemus (general)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 316 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eudemus was a Macedonian officer whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> left in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> after his campaign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. After Alexander's death he took control of the region and murdered the Indian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porus">Porus</a> around 317 BCE. He then joined Eumenes in his war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a>, bringing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a> from India, and was executed by Antigonus after Eumenes' defeat in 316 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eudemus-general.jpg" alt="Eudemus (general)" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. World Imaging assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EasternSatrapsAfterAlexander.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
